  "methodology": "Screening uses the first window_fraction of lots in timestamp order (both classes); no Phase II lot informs any statistic, rank, or redundancy decision. Per sensor: point-biserial r, two-sample KS, two-sided Mann-Whitney U, and Cohen-style d (fail minus pass over pooled SD), all on pairwise-complete observations. Benjamini-Hochberg FDR is applied separately to the KS and Mann-Whitney p-value families. Sensors rank by mean rank across |r|, KS statistic, |d|, and min(q_ks, q_mw) (rankdata average ties, sensor code breaks order ties). Greedy redundancy: walking rank order, a sensor is marked redundant with the first already-retained sensor whose absolute window correlation exceeds the threshold. Selection walks retained sensors in rank order, taking significant (q < alpha) sensors with |d| >= effect_floor up to max_selected; if fewer than min_selected qualify, the top retained sensors fill to min_selected (counted as floor_filled) so downstream SPC has a usable input set.",
